From dbd50805909cd9bb6689227df0e3c85fb904868c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Solbjor <thomas.solbjor@fortedigital.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 10:35:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Make UpCloud deployment-ready: object storage for
 Loki/Velero, deploy guards
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

UpCloud previously came up degraded: Loki on a throwaway PVC, Velero
never installed (so Forgejo's volume and Vault's snapshots had no
backup), and a fresh deploy failed outright because external-dns's
--atomic install waited on a Cloudflare token secret nothing had
created.

- tofu/upcloud: buckets <prefix>-loki and <prefix>-velero, one
  object-storage user each with a bucket-scoped policy and access key
  — UpCloud has no workload identity, so scoped keys are the ceiling.
  Keys flow through gitignored secrets.env into Kubernetes Secrets;
  they never enter values files or the published GitOps repo.
- deploy.sh: upcloud arms for the Loki overlay and Velero target,
  creates both credential Secrets, and skips external-dns with
  instructions instead of rolling back the deploy when the Cloudflare
  secret is missing.
- New upcloud overlays: Loki S3 backend (creds via the AWS env-var
  chain), Velero with the aws plugin against the S3-compatible
  endpoint and kopia FS backup — no snapshot plugin exists, and FS
  backup cannot reach unmounted PVCs (documented in OPERATIONS.md).
- quickstart: the upcloud DNS-zone detector checked a secret in a
  cluster that does not exist yet at that step, wedging
  --run-remaining-steps; it now checks public NS delegation.
- Docs: UPCLOUD_SETUP.md claimed KMS auto-unseal (UpCloud has none —
  3-of-5 manual keys) and an api_allowed_cidrs=[] example the module
  rejects; all *_SETUP.md gain the gitops-repo and validate --e2e
  steps; CLOUD_CAPABILITIES.md gap section rewritten to what remains.
- Cleanup: dead tofu/scripts/ (wrong env vars, nonexistent outputs),
  orphaned pre-Gateway cluster-issuer.yaml, stale GitLab/nginx
  comments.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
